{
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/sarif-2.1/schema/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "fullName": "Trivy Vulnerability Scanner",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy",
          "name": "Trivy",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-3605",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Vault: Vault: Denial of Service due to unauthorized secret deletion via policy bypass"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An authenticated user with access to a kvv2 path through a policy containing a glob may be able to delete secrets they were not authorized to read or write, resulting in denial-of-service. This vulnerability did not allow a malicious user to delete secrets across namespaces, nor read any secret data. Fxed in Vault Community Edition 2.0.0 and Vault Enterprise 2.0.0, 1.21.5, 1.20.10, and 1.19.16."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-3605",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-3605\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: github.com/hashicorp/vault\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-3605](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-3605)\nAn authenticated user with access to a kvv2 path through a policy containing a glob may be able to delete secrets they were not authorized to read or write, resulting in denial-of-service. This vulnerability did not allow a malicious user to delete secrets across namespaces, nor read any secret data. Fxed in Vault Community Edition 2.0.0 and Vault Enterprise 2.0.0, 1.21.5, 1.20.10, and 1.19.16.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-3605**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|github.com/hashicorp/vault||[CVE-2026-3605](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-3605)|\n\nAn authenticated user with access to a kvv2 path through a policy containing a glob may be able to delete secrets they were not authorized to read or write, resulting in denial-of-service. This vulnerability did not allow a malicious user to delete secrets across namespaces, nor read any secret data. Fxed in Vault Community Edition 2.0.0 and Vault Enterprise 2.0.0, 1.21.5, 1.20.10, and 1.19.16."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 8.1,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:H",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.1",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-4525",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Vault: Vault: Information disclosure of authentication tokens via incorrect header handling"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "If a Vault auth mount is configured to pass through the \"Authorization\" header, and the \"Authorization\" header is used to authenticate to Vault, Vault forwarded the Vault token to the auth plugin backend. Fixed in 2.0.0, 1.21.5, 1.20.10, and 1.19.16."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-4525",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-4525\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: github.com/hashicorp/vault\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-4525](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-4525)\nIf a Vault auth mount is configured to pass through the \"Authorization\" header, and the \"Authorization\" header is used to authenticate to Vault, Vault forwarded the Vault token to the auth plugin backend. Fixed in 2.0.0, 1.21.5, 1.20.10, and 1.19.16.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-4525**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|github.com/hashicorp/vault||[CVE-2026-4525](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-4525)|\n\nIf a Vault auth mount is configured to pass through the \"Authorization\" header, and the \"Authorization\" header is used to authenticate to Vault, Vault forwarded the Vault token to the auth plugin backend. Fixed in 2.0.0, 1.21.5, 1.20.10, and 1.19.16."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 7.5,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "7.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-5807",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Vault: Vault: Denial of Service via unauthenticated root token generation or rekey operations"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Vault is vulnerable to a denial-of-service condition where an unauthenticated attacker can repeatedly initiate or cancel root token generation or rekey operations, occupying the single in-progress operation slot. This prevents legitimate operators from completing these workflows. This vulnerability, CVE-2026-5807, is fixed in Vault Community Edition 2.0.0 and Vault Enterprise 2.0.0."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-5807",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-5807\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: github.com/hashicorp/vault\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-5807](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-5807)\nVault is vulnerable to a denial-of-service condition where an unauthenticated attacker can repeatedly initiate or cancel root token generation or rekey operations, occupying the single in-progress operation slot. This prevents legitimate operators from completing these workflows. This vulnerability, CVE-2026-5807, is fixed in Vault Community Edition 2.0.0 and Vault Enterprise 2.0.0.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-5807**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|github.com/hashicorp/vault||[CVE-2026-5807](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-5807)|\n\nVault is vulnerable to a denial-of-service condition where an unauthenticated attacker can repeatedly initiate or cancel root token generation or rekey operations, occupying the single in-progress operation slot. This prevents legitimate operators from completing these workflows. This vulnerability, CVE-2026-5807, is fixed in Vault Community Edition 2.0.0 and Vault Enterprise 2.0.0."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 7.5,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "7.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-5052",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Vault: Vault: Information disclosure via Server-Side Request Forgery in ACME challenge validation"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Vault’s PKI engine’s ACME validation did not reject local targets when issuing http-01 and tls-alpn-01 challenges. This may lead to these requests being sent to local network targets, potentially leading to information disclosure. Fixed in Vault Community Edition 2.0.0 and Vault Enterprise 2.0.0, 1.21.5, 1.20.10, and 1.19.16."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-5052",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-5052\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: github.com/hashicorp/vault\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-5052](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-5052)\nVault’s PKI engine’s ACME validation did not reject local targets when issuing http-01 and tls-alpn-01 challenges. This may lead to these requests being sent to local network targets, potentially leading to information disclosure. Fixed in Vault Community Edition 2.0.0 and Vault Enterprise 2.0.0, 1.21.5, 1.20.10, and 1.19.16.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-5052**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|github.com/hashicorp/vault||[CVE-2026-5052](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-5052)|\n\nVault’s PKI engine’s ACME validation did not reject local targets when issuing http-01 and tls-alpn-01 challenges. This may lead to these requests being sent to local network targets, potentially leading to information disclosure. Fixed in Vault Community Edition 2.0.0 and Vault Enterprise 2.0.0, 1.21.5, 1.20.10, and 1.19.16."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 5.3,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.3",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-41889",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "github.com/jackc/pgx: golang: pgx: SQL injection via specific SQL query conditions"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "pgx is a PostgreSQL driver and toolkit for Go. Prior to version 5.9.2, SQL injection can occur when the non-default simple protocol is used, a dollar quoted string literal is used in the SQL query, that string literal contains text that would be would be interpreted as a placeholder outside of a string literal, and the value of that placeholder is controllable by the attacker. This issue has been patched in version 5.9.2."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-41889",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-41889\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: github.com/jackc/pgx/v5\nFixed Version: 5.9.2\nLink: [CVE-2026-41889](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-41889)\npgx is a PostgreSQL driver and toolkit for Go. Prior to version 5.9.2, SQL injection can occur when the non-default simple protocol is used, a dollar quoted string literal is used in the SQL query, that string literal contains text that would be would be interpreted as a placeholder outside of a string literal, and the value of that placeholder is controllable by the attacker. This issue has been patched in version 5.9.2.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-41889**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|github.com/jackc/pgx/v5|5.9.2|[CVE-2026-41889](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-41889)|\n\npgx is a PostgreSQL driver and toolkit for Go. Prior to version 5.9.2, SQL injection can occur when the non-default simple protocol is used, a dollar quoted string literal is used in the SQL query, that string literal contains text that would be would be interpreted as a placeholder outside of a string literal, and the value of that placeholder is controllable by the attacker. This issue has been patched in version 5.9.2."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv40_baseScore": 2.3,
                "cvssv40_vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-2303",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-2303 affecting package telegraf for versions less than 1.29.4-21"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The mongo-go-driver repository contains CGo bindings for GSSAPI (Kerberos) authentication on Linux and macOS. The C wrapper implementation contains a heap out-of-bounds read vulnerability due to incorrect assumptions about string termination in the GSSAPI standard. Since GSSAPI buffers are not guaranteed to be null-terminated or have extra padding, this results in reading one byte past the allocated heap buffer."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-2303",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-2303\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: go.mongodb.org/mongo-driver/v2\nFixed Version: 2.4.2\nLink: [CVE-2026-2303](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-2303)\nThe mongo-go-driver repository contains CGo bindings for GSSAPI (Kerberos) authentication on Linux and macOS. The C wrapper implementation contains a heap out-of-bounds read vulnerability due to incorrect assumptions about string termination in the GSSAPI standard. Since GSSAPI buffers are not guaranteed to be null-terminated or have extra padding, this results in reading one byte past the allocated heap buffer.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-2303**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|go.mongodb.org/mongo-driver/v2|2.4.2|[CVE-2026-2303](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-2303)|\n\nThe mongo-go-driver repository contains CGo bindings for GSSAPI (Kerberos) authentication on Linux and macOS. The C wrapper implementation contains a heap out-of-bounds read vulnerability due to incorrect assumptions about string termination in the GSSAPI standard. Since GSSAPI buffers are not guaranteed to be null-terminated or have extra padding, this results in reading one byte past the allocated heap buffer."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 6.5,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:N",
                "cvssv40_baseScore": 6.9,
                "cvssv40_vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:P/VC:N/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "6.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2026-5932",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "The golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp package is unmaintained, unsafe by design, and has known security issues"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp package is unsafe by design, has numerous known security issues, is not maintained, and should not be used.\n\nIf you are required to interoperate with OpenPGP systems and need a maintained package, consider github.com/ProtonMail/go-crypto/openpgp which is a maintained fork that aims to be a drop-in replacement for this package."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability GO-2026-5932\nSeverity: UNKNOWN\nPackage: golang.org/x/crypto\nFixed Version: \nLink: [GO-2026-5932]()\nThe golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp package is unsafe by design, has numerous known security issues, is not maintained, and should not be used.\n\nIf you are required to interoperate with OpenPGP systems and need a maintained package, consider github.com/ProtonMail/go-crypto/openpgp which is a maintained fork that aims to be a drop-in replacement for this package.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability GO-2026-5932**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|UNKNOWN|golang.org/x/crypto||[GO-2026-5932]()|\n\nThe golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp package is unsafe by design, has numerous known security issues, is not maintained, and should not be used.\n\nIf you are required to interoperate with OpenPGP systems and need a maintained package, consider github.com/ProtonMail/go-crypto/openpgp which is a maintained fork that aims to be a drop-in replacement for this package."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "0.0",
                "tags": [
